Package: slipcase-desktop
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/excelano/slipcase-desktop
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libegl1, libvulkan1 | libgl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxi6, libxcursor1, libxrandr2, shared-mime-info, desktop-file-utils, hicolor-icon-theme
Description: Viewer and metadata editor for slipcase containers
 Opens a .slpc container, shows its metadata as an editable tree, and hands
 the payload to whatever application the desktop has registered for it.
 .
 The container format is read and written entirely through the slpc library,
 which is the reference implementation of the slipcase specification. This
 application parses no containers of its own.
 .
 Only two of the libraries above are found by dpkg-shlibdeps. The executable
 links libc and libgcc and nothing else; the display stack, the graphics
 driver loader, and the keyboard map library are all opened by name at run
 time, so a package built from the linker's answer alone would install on a
 machine where it cannot start. The three tool packages at the end own the
 dpkg triggers that rebuild the mime, desktop, and icon caches, which is why
 this package carries no maintainer scripts.
